{"_v":1,"id":"the-unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-west-end-2026","bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Dominic Cavendish","o":"The Telegraph","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/the-unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-review-west-end/","d":"2026-02-15","q":"Its sadness rings true, while its crowd-pleasing positivity is hedged with knowing make-believe."},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/the-unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-theatre-royal-haymarket-review-b1270389.html","d":"2026-02-11","q":"Yet for all its obvious charms and consummate professionalism it remains curiously uninvolving and slight."},{"cn":"Olivia Rook","o":"London Theatre","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/the-unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-review-rachel-joyce-passenger-mark-addy","d":"2026-02-11","q":"Adapted for the stage by Rachel Joyce from her 2012 novel, with a brilliant score by Passenger, this new musical is a profoundly moving celebration of hope."},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-musical-review-theatre-royal-haymarket-b2917524.html?callback=in&amp;code=YJNMNZLMNJITZTFIOC0ZMGYZLWE4ZDCTMTGYYZG3ODAYNWQ1&amp;state=14c70dbe8df94df68da61a67b37a9c34","d":"2026-02-15","q":"It takes you on a journey that sends you home feeling a bit lighter, a bit more hopeful, than you did before."},{"cn":"Paul Vale","o":"The Stage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/the-unlikely-pilgrimage-of-harold-fry-review-theatre-royal-haymarket-london","d":"2026-02-15","q":"Joyce's rather sentimental story blossoms as a musical, with Passenger's diverse score enhancing those underlying themes."}],"au":{"score":84,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":84,"c":2